From a6953a43086fb6b11ccde806cfb01969c518a183 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Iustin Ventaniuc <iustiniv@google.com>
Date: Sun, 21 Jun 2026 01:22:22 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 13/17] Fix boot-loop vulnerability in setPermissionGrantState

A malicious BYOD work-profile DPC could persistently boot-loop the device by passing an out-of-range `grantState` to `setPermissionGrantState()`. This unvalidated value was saved to disk and threw an uncaught `IllegalArgumentException` during subsequent `system_server` boots, requiring a factory reset.

This commit fixes the issue by:
1. Adding a `Preconditions.checkArgument` in `DevicePolicyManagerService` to validate the `grantState` when the coexistence flag is enabled, preventing invalid states from being stored.
2. Wrapping policy re-application calls in `DevicePolicyEngine` with try-catch blocks to ensure that any invalid saved policy state logs a non-fatal error instead of crashing the `system_server` during boot.

Test: Added and ran testSetPermissionGrantState_coexistence_invalidState_throwsException in DevicePolicyManagerTest

